# Sabor-app: project structure

This file describes the physical folder structure of the project.
Use it to place new files in correct locations.

Root structure:
- frontend/  -> React frontend (UI)
- backend/   -> Flask backend (API, auth, DB)
- .cursor/   -> Cursor project rules
- README.md  -> project documentation

Frontend structure:
- frontend/src/
  - pages/        -> React pages used by React Router
  - components/   -> Reusable UI components
  - services/     -> API / fetch helpers
  - assets/       -> Images, icons, static assets
  - App.js        -> Main app + routing
  - index.js      -> React entry point

Backend structure:
- backend/
  - app.py        -> Flask app entry point
  - routes/       -> API route definitions
  - models/       -> Database models (SQLAlchemy)
  - services/     -> Business logic
  - static/       -> Uploaded/static files (if any)
  - templates/    -> HTML templates (if used)

Rules:
- Do NOT mix frontend and backend code.
- Do NOT create new top-level folders without a clear reason.
- Place new files into existing folders whenever possible.